1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:02,160
This humanoid can do a backflip.

2
00:00:02,160 --> 00:00:04,160
It cannot put a block in a box.

3
00:00:04,160 --> 00:00:06,280
We gave it a brain, and a name.

4
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:06,960
Box.

5
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:07,240
Off.

6
00:00:07,240 --> 00:00:08,000
Ice.

7
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,050
Box Office.

8
00:00:09,353 --> 00:00:12,313
Three to five objects lie on the counter.

9
00:00:12,313 --> 00:00:15,953
Cubes, cylinders and prisms,
in red, yellow and blue.

10
00:00:15,953 --> 00:00:17,993
Three boxes wait behind them.

11
00:00:17,993 --> 00:00:19,873
The robot has two minutes.

12
00:00:19,873 --> 00:00:21,753
A right box earns points.

13
00:00:21,753 --> 00:00:23,673
A wrong box costs one.

14
00:00:23,673 --> 00:00:25,963
So when it is unsure, it skips.

15
00:00:26,187 --> 00:00:29,527
A person says where things
go, in their own words.

16
00:00:29,527 --> 00:00:31,307
The blue ones in between.

17
00:00:31,307 --> 00:00:33,367
The first box from the left.

18
00:00:33,367 --> 00:00:35,387
Our parser has no templates.

19
00:00:35,387 --> 00:00:38,517
It turns each sentence
into one box per object.

20
00:00:38,787 --> 00:00:42,087
Aalto published real
recordings from the venue.

21
00:00:42,087 --> 00:00:45,767
On those frames, the stock
colour rules saw the orange boxes

22
00:00:45,767 --> 00:00:50,067
and the robot's hands as objects,
and missed the red ones.

23
00:00:50,067 --> 00:00:51,727
We fixed the colours.

24
00:00:51,727 --> 00:00:53,547
Detections fell from one hundred thirty-two

25
00:00:53,547 --> 00:00:56,917
to seventy-four, about five per frame.

26
00:00:57,153 --> 00:00:59,673
The camera calibration was off too.

27
00:00:59,673 --> 00:01:02,693
The table looked tilted by fourteen degrees.

28
00:01:02,693 --> 00:01:06,413
Now the robot measures the
table itself, and levels it.

29
00:01:06,413 --> 00:01:09,903
Objects read about forty-five
millimetres tall again.

30
00:01:10,087 --> 00:01:14,187
We scored it in Aalto's
simulator, on randomised scenes.

31
00:01:14,187 --> 00:01:17,807
Fixed sorting: ten of twenty
objects, up from eight.

32
00:01:17,807 --> 00:01:20,287
By instruction: ten of eighteen.

33
00:01:20,287 --> 00:01:22,547
Not one object went into a wrong box,

34
00:01:22,547 --> 00:01:25,547
and the safety filter
never clipped a command.

35
00:01:25,547 --> 00:01:28,267
On the real recordings,
the robot starts moving

36
00:01:28,267 --> 00:01:31,177
after about one second, not up to fifty-two.

